            <ArticleTitle>Surgical management of multiple painful rib nonunions in patient with a history of severe shoulder girdle trauma: a case report and literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>600-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/BOT.0b013e3181a15e90</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report painful nonunions after multiple rib fractures in a 50-year-old man who sustained a displaced scapula fracture and multiple ipsilateral rib fractures. The rib nonunions were reconstructed after an 11-month trial of nonoperative management, which was unsuccessful. The nonunions healed and symptoms completely resolved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
